          "Check whether the exception came from a form, a rule, or a permission. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. Do not close a case just because the requester stopped asking. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. The {topic} record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from backup roster and access test.",
          "Record the stop reason and the release decision together. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Route one bounded question to the owner instead of negotiating in the queue. If the exception repeats, give it a reason code. In this {topic} case, the record points to the scheduling platform and names the engagement manager as the decision owner."
